## The article (already published, English version, https://matthieuhuguet.com/reels/louisiana-bayou-church-the-roof)
Title: "Louisiana Bayou Church: The Roof". Subtitle: "Procedural roof geometry, UV variations and Copernicus heightmaps". Banner: "Main film coming soon".
- Step 1, geometry: a regular grid of roof tiles; every other row offset by half a tile so the seams fall in the middle of the tiles beside them; rows overlap so each tile covers part of the one below; in Houdini an HDA with a slider controls the number of tiles.
- Step 2, texture density: general guide 1,024 px per metre for a hero asset, 512 px per metre for an asset seen from a distance, 2,048 px per metre for a character (depends on the final render). The roof is measured in metres, the density needed per tile is calculated. The surface is relatively flat, so one 2,048 px square sheet holds 36 patterns in a 6 by 6 grid; four orientations let the patterns be reused while keeping sharpness. Tiles are not all square: a pattern is revealed beneath each tile to suggest its lower edge, then each tile's UVs are adjusted until the layout looks right.
- Step 3, variations: for each tile generated by the HDA, one of the 36 patterns is chosen at random (VEX), its UVs are moved to the matching cell, then one of four orientations is used: normal, mirrored horizontally, mirrored vertically, rotated 180 degrees. The roof is coloured by pattern slot to check the assignment.
- Heightmaps made with a Copernicus graph (Houdini) for: windows and stairs, white paint for the main wooden parts, roof tile variations.

## The film (new, rendered directly in Unreal Engine)
- Unreal Engine 5.8, rendered with Movie Render Queue, lit with Lumen. 24 fps, 21:9, 3,360 x 1,440 (also cropped to 9:16 and 1:1).
- The scene is the Louisiana Bayou church, imported from Houdini into Unreal. Only 3 materials, all with 2,048 px textures: (1) white painting; (2) window and wood, variations A, B and the stair share the same texture; (3) the roof tiles, a trim sheet.
- Environment in the scene: procedural grass laid with a PCG graph on a circular ground, volumetric clouds from the Ultra Dynamic Sky plugin with a matte painting sky, and fog actors scattered around.
- Timing measured on a test: about 0.9 s per frame at 3,360 x 1,440 (0.52 s per frame at 2,520 x 1,080). The full film is 960 frames of render (40 s of shots) inside a 46 s montage.
- The film opens on the first shot, then a motion title (date 29 October 2026, "Louisiana Bayou Church"), the shots continue, and the title returns over the church from 9 s to 17 s.
- Music: "Lumière's Opera : Nuit sur Lumière" by Lorien Testard (Clair Obscur: Expedition 33) then "Aerith's Theme" (Final Fantasy VII Remake). Wind ambience from a YouTube ambience video.
